@startuml
title Invocation states, refusal and recovery (not session records)

state "CURRENT interactive API - SPEC 0.5.0-draft" as Current {
  state "Read / validate config\ncurator-run, caller identity" as Config
  state "Normalize / validate argv" as Args
  state "Resolve / repair\nCurator subprocess, caller-side" as Resolve
  state "Map / defaults / host / permissions\nhosted resume / stdin / terminal gates" as Validate
  state "Build admitted plan\nagents-management in-process" as Plan
  state "Provider-limit gate\noptional native network admission" as Network
  state "Compose / project value" as Compose
  state "Native late checks\nbinary, MCP layer, prompt" as Late
  state "Direct execution / wait\ncurator-run owns child / terminal restoration" as Execute
  state "ax handoff\nax start subprocess" as Ax
  state "Accepted ax handoff\nax owns process / terminal / Session Record" as Accepted
  state "Hosted receiver / wait\ntask-board owns terminal / deadlines / completion" as Hosted
  state "Refused\nterminal invocation; no weaker launch" as Refused
  state "Exited\nchild status or classified receiver result" as Exited
  [*] --> Config
  Config --> Args : valid config; enabled / disabled / absent ax routes explicitly
  Config --> Refused : unreadable / malformed / unsafe file
  Args --> Resolve : accepted interactive invocation
  Args --> Refused : usage / unknown flags / locked override
  Args --> Exited : accepted help / version (0)
  Resolve --> Validate : closed v1 / v2 / v3 fragment
  Resolve --> Refused : resolve / repair / lock / fragment failure
  Validate --> Plan : supported mapping / posture / host
  Validate --> Refused : unsupported mapping / permission / hosted capability\nconflict, machine hosted default or invalid resume / terminal
  Plan --> Network : admitted plan; no process created
  Plan --> Refused : unsupported mode / model / effort / release / context collision
  Network --> Compose : serviceable verdict; optional network admitted
  Network --> Refused : failed / unknown verdict; limited provider; network refusal
  Compose --> Late : native (direct or ax)
  Compose --> Hosted : valid hosted payload / transport
  Compose --> Refused : payload / stdin / composition invalid
  Late --> Refused : first binary / MCP / prompt failure
  Late --> Execute : direct route
  Late --> Ax : configured ax, no explicit native bypass
  Execute --> Exited : waits; forwards signals / stop-continue\nrestores terminal; exit or 128 + signal
  Ax --> Refused : cannot start / rejects / nonzero; no direct fallback
  Ax --> Accepted : accepted handoff; launch work ends
  Hosted --> Refused : missing receiver / valid refusal / protocol or transport loss
  Hosted --> Exited : no refusal record; receiver exit unchanged
  Refused --> [*]
  Exited --> [*]
  Accepted --> [*]
}
note right of Current
  [[../SPEC.md#1-scope-and-non-goals SPEC 1]] / [[../SPEC.md#4-composition-algorithm SPEC 4]] / [[../SPEC.md#46-hand-off-and-exec SPEC 4.6]] / [[../SPEC.md#49-hosted-payload-and-receiver-handoff SPEC 4.9]] / [[../SPEC.md#6-errors-and-diagnostics SPEC 6]].
  States are per-invocation descriptions, not a persisted launcher FSM.
  Current launcher owns no leases, checkpoints, resume records or session memory.
  Config is launcher-owned; homes / profiles are Curator-owned;
  ax owns its Session Record. Hosted durable layout / destination UID:
  unspecified in spec 4.9. Direct terminal / wait behavior:
  [[../README.md#environment-and-transport README Environment and transport]].
  Refusal has no outgoing retry transition: operator deliberately starts a new invocation.
  New resolve --repair can restore a missing MCP layer; launcher never repairs it.
end note

state "TARGET one-shot - NOT IMPLEMENTED; dispatcher v0 local headless" as Target {
  state "Caller composes immutable plan\ncaller-side identity" as CallerPlan
  state "Dispatcher intake / admission\nservice UID unspecified in spec 10.2" as Intake
  state "Provision / bind / claim\ndispatcher owns durable execution state" as Provision
  state "Materialize admitted B / resources\napproved child-UID executor; dispatcher workspace contract" as Materialize
  state "Privileged checks / atomic start receipt\nswarma-user-launcher, root" as RootCheck
  state "User-manager lifecycle / approved exec\ncaller-owned 0-2 and read-only plan FD3 only" as Drop
  state "Verify intake / destination binding\ncurator-run under agent UID worker-<label>" as Verify
  state "Selected-source qualification / lease\nagent executor; broker checks peer / grants" as Lease
  state "Recheck binding / execute harness\nagent UID; execution-scoped credential" as Harness
  state "Execution outcome evidence\ndispatcher / supervisor owns record" as Outcome
  state "Owned exec.stop\nroot user-manager helper\nlatest receipt authority; all UID processes / service domain\nTERM / grace / KILL; recorded stop replays without signals" as Stop
  state "Account-wide absence confirmed\nquiet period; escaped descendants included" as Absent
  state "Unknown / contradictory process evidence\nno claim release / replacement" as Unknown
  state "Export manifest-relative change set\napproved child UID; fixed env / no network\nworkspace write-fenced where applicable" as Export
  state "Export recorded / result resource\noriginal caller only; board imports / reviews exact C / integrates" as Exported
  state "Export obligation retained\nno home deletion; explicit operator waiver possible" as ExportHeld
  state "Unbind then retire / delete home\nquiesce / declared-key cleanup; confirmed effects" as Cleanup
  state "Target refusal\nnon-success, typed metadata; no fallback" as TargetRefusal
  state "Account retired\noptional separate registered one-shot revocation" as Retired
  [*] --> CallerPlan
  CallerPlan --> Intake : already composed immutable plan, no secrets
  Intake --> TargetRefusal : size / authority / capacity / unsupported v0 shape
  Intake --> Provision : admitted; smallest path bound before provisioning
  Provision --> Materialize : workspace-capable allocation
  Materialize --> RootCheck : materialized; owned claim / approved executor
  Materialize --> TargetRefusal : invalid archive / materialization failure
  Provision --> RootCheck : non-workspace allocation only
  RootCheck --> TargetRefusal : inactive / unowned / unapproved / digest / duplicate receipt
  RootCheck --> Drop : write receipt BEFORE privilege drop
  Drop --> TargetRefusal : privilege_drop_failed
  Drop --> Verify : agent-side executor reads bounded plan once
  Verify --> TargetRefusal : missing / bad / unknown intake or digest / binding / surface drift
  Verify --> Lease : verified immutable values; no profile repair / model choice
  Lease --> TargetRefusal : source conflict / broker unavailable / ledger / grants\nbinding / harness / channel / qualification refusal
  Lease --> Harness : source policy admits; qualified broker lease if selected
  Harness --> TargetRefusal : recheck / renewal or authentication failure
  Harness --> Outcome : required evidence; exact transport unpublished
  Harness --> Stop : dispatcher cancellation / max runtime / permitted host_stop
  Outcome --> Stop : when owned stop needed; exit alone is not absence
  Outcome --> Unknown : evidence unknown / contradictory
  Stop --> Unknown : processes_remain / no confirmed termination receipt
  Stop --> Absent : verified termination receipt
  Absent --> Export : workspace round ended; write fence where applicable
  Export --> Exported : whole export admitted; digests journaled
  Export --> ExportHeld : unsafe paths / collisions / special files / cap / unknown
  Exported --> Cleanup : export recorded; confirmed cleanup effects only
  ExportHeld --> Cleanup : explicit operator act waives export; confirmed effects only
  Absent --> Cleanup : non-workspace allocation only; confirmed effects
  Cleanup --> Retired : unbind then account retirement confirmed
  TargetRefusal --> [*] : terminal for invocation; dispatcher still owns cleanup obligations
  Retired --> [*]
}
note right of Target
  [[../SPEC.md#101-immutable-input-descriptor-transport-and-limits SPEC 10.1]] / [[../SPEC.md#102-caller-dispatcher-privileged-launcher-and-executor SPEC 10.2]] / [[../SPEC.md#103-broker-binding-credential-delivery-and-rollout SPEC 10.3]] / [[../SPEC.md#104-signals-stop-receipts-and-cleanup SPEC 10.4]] / [[../SPEC.md#105-typed-refusals-exit-status-and-activation-questions SPEC 10.5]].
  This is an obligation map, not a new persisted state schema.
  No autonomous recovery transition from Unknown is defined here:
  recovery procedure unspecified in spec 10.4; no inferred capacity release.
  Start receipt proves attempt / identity, not readiness.
  Consumed-plan / exit wire, post-exec renewal / release ownership,
  numeric refusal exits and signal encoding: unspecified in spec 10.4-10.5.
  Claude setup-token expiry / auth failure: re-enroll and restart; no refresh.
  Later Codex renewal: 8 s timeout fails turn, no late response / login fallback.
  Unix-socket service from first slice; SH2 host_start / host_stop / permit needs publication;
  Service unavailable / unready refuses; queue / events / long waits later on same transport.
  FD3 mechanism, intake / digest / framing / read deadline: publication gates in SPEC 10.1.
  User-manager spec 7 / diagrams/launch.puml owns lifecycle; no internal handles in executor.
  Prefer completely staged bounded immutable bytes; pipe needs capacity / feeder / deadline / cleanup.
  SH2 host admission permit: session-scoped for one logical_session_id.
  Session lifecycle authorisation member unpublished; successors require authorisation / previous-claim absence.
  host_start idempotent per (logical_session_id, op_id); each physical start keeps its own claim / fence / receipt.
  Physical interlock: (execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id); only dispatcher invokes root.
  Fence changes prevent stale start / reconcile; host_stop under permit uses journaled E-stop / confirmed absence.
  host_stop: configured host principal only, host-requested, distinct from owner cancel; no start authority.
  Ambiguous start resolves same effect / receipt, no second launch; stop if required.
  Runner authenticates fresh host channel; epoch registration / readiness before delivery.
  R-TRANSFER workspace export precedes retirement; recorded export or operator waiver before deletion.
  Separate retirement metadata export: service-generated closed schema only.
  Separate operator home retention has no confidentiality guarantee.
  Single stop / retirement termination scope: user-manager spec 4.4 / 4.7; old receipt cannot stop successor.
  Process fate table / replaced-daemon writer fence: user-manager spec 7 (R-FATE); no live supervisor adoption.
  Cross-account workspace: standalone repository with private .git / common directory / refs / index / fresh config; no hooks.
  No inherited .git backlink / executable local config / credential helpers; copy / reflink preserves rule.
  Linked worktrees within one account only; shared objects immutable / read-only; formats open (SPEC 10.5).
  R-TIME: authenticated / operator-controlled installer time source; durable dispatcher / broker watermark.
  Expiry max(now, watermark); not_before min(now, watermark); no untrusted advance; operator reset.
  Expiry-driven home / binding destruction also requires boot-inclusive monotonic elapsed lifetime.
  no remote / native resume / seeded continuity in dispatcher v0.
end note
note right of Verify
  Wave-5 launch obligations - SPEC 10.1-10.2 / 10.6
  R-TRANSFER: plan digest covers B / manifest digest / write scope / exec-profile reference.
  R-NET-TOOL: read-only task resources covered by digest; bound provider proxy only.
  No web by default; plan disables provider-side search, invisible to network rules.
  Only operator-granted trusted-circle opt-in: qualified server search or platform Unix-socket web service.
  R-STANDING: verify settings / hooks / MCP / instructions by digest before exec, or root-owned surfaces.
  Drift refuses (code unpublished); repair is explicit re-materialization.
  R-EXEC: D-PATH protected light-check wrappers / fixed subcommands; no heavy entry points.
  User manager owns OS exec allowlist; R-VERIFY builds / tests / code execution on another machine.
  R-UNTRUSTED refused in Slice 0 / user-manager v0; workplace zero egress / donor-side loop.
  Admission: R-CEILINGS / R-WATCH / R-ALLSTOP / R-RANGE-DENY / R-SOCKETS / R-SHARED (SPEC 10.6).
  Exact plan / transfer / opt-in formats and qualification remain open; no implementation claimed.
end note
@enduml
